---
config:
  flowchart:
    wrappingWidth: 400
---
flowchart TB
    accTitle: The check of the log of Nextcloud
    accDescr: At its end, run.sh pipes the log of Nextcloud, which holds every record of PHP and of the app at debug, into assert_log.py, which counts the records at each level. A record that the app didn't write and whose message, exception and data name neither a file of the app nor its namespace passes. A record of the app fails the check when it is a deprecation, notice or warning of PHP in a file of the app, an error or a fatal error, or a warning that no test provokes on purpose; every other record of the app passes. Each finding names its place in the files of the app, its request and the record.

    log["data/nextcloud.log<br>every record of PHP and of the app<br>at debug, through log.condition"]
    check["assert_log.py<br>counts the records at each level"]
    app{"A record<br>of the app?"}
    other["passes:<br>a record of core<br>or of another app"]
    php{"A deprecation, notice<br>or warning of PHP<br>in a file of the app?"}
    error{"An error or<br>a fatal error?"}
    warning{"A warning that<br>no test provokes?"}
    fine["passes"]
    failed["the check fails<br>with the place in the files of the app,<br>the request and the record"]

    log --> check --> app
    app -- "no" --> other
    app -- "yes" --> php
    php -- "yes" --> failed
    php -- "no" --> error
    error -- "yes" --> failed
    error -- "no" --> warning
    warning -- "yes" --> failed
    warning -- "no" --> fine

    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    classDef fail fill:#dc26262e,stroke:#dc2626,stroke-width:2px
    class log,check bot
    class other,fine done
    class failed fail
